  WLOG, set <math|a\<gtr\>b>, if <math|a\<less\>b>, <math|a,b=b,a>%b=b,a.

  Then: <math|a=bk<rsub|1>+r<rsub|1>,b=r<rsub|1>k<rsub|2>+r<rsub|2>\<ldots\>> Bezout Theorem can show <math|\<exists\>r<rsub|n>,r<rsub|n+1>>, <math|u,v\<in\>\<bbb-Z\>>,s.t.\ 

